          "explanation": "$y(t) = AB \\times$ (length of overlap of $x(\\tau)$ on $[0, {{T1}}]$ and $h(t - \\tau)$ on $[t - {{T2}}, t]$). At $t = {{t0}}$ the overlap runs from {{max(0,t0-T2)}} to {{min(t0,T1)}}: length {{max(0, min(t0,T1) - max(0, t0-T2))}} s. So $y = {{A}}\\cdot{{B}}\\cdot{{max(0, min(t0,T1) - max(0, t0-T2))}}$ = {{A*B*max(0, min(t0,T1) - max(0, t0-T2))}}.",
